XSA_PLAN_V2_WITNESS witness stream = 8B x chi; chi/n = 0.283 is the 1GB FIXTURE ratio (the pile value is unmeasured): ~0 GB at this scale; if it exceeds --wit-ram-budget the overflow spills as sorted varint-delta disc runs (est. <= 0.3x raw, EXTRAPOLATED - unmeasured at spill scale) inside the tree
XSA_PLAN_V2_TRANSIENT no chunk set, no merge transient, no persistent position column: the producer's scratch is the piece window (0.062 GiB, W=1100 bands x 65536 runs), the rlebwt it is publishing (0.0 GiB) and the ROLLING WINDOW FILES (0.0 GiB on disc = 2 credit x cap x 8 B, one file per live window, unlinked the moment its bins are built); the build's RAM is one group (0.0 GiB, 16 B/slot) and NEVER the window; inputs the finish consumes are unlinked as read; witness spill reserve 0.0 GiB (0.3x overflow, EXTRAPOLATED)
XSA_PLAN_V2_CAP live_cap_slots=2088968 source=auto from --memory-gb 16 (bound by address space) bound_by=address space (--memory-gb): corpus cache + fill staging + 16 B/slot arena pair; MEMORY bound: 90% of --memory-gb 16 GiB (17179869184 B) = 15461882265 B usable - corpus cache 2088968 B (min(n, 512 B x pool slots 1048576)) - staging 167772160 B (4 threads x (33554432 B fill + 8388608 B leaf)) = 15292021137 B / 16 B per build-group slot = 955751321 slots; SCRATCH bound: 90% of 751.9 GiB free = 726596241408 B - rlebwt+pieces 70076520 B = 726526164888 B / (credit 2 x 8 B per slot) = 2088968 slots; window_file_gb=0.03 = credit x cap x 8 B ON DISC (0 B of address space: the fill writes with buffered pwrite, never a mapping); the finish is its own process under the same cap: witness 0.0 GiB fits it, headroom_pct=90
XSA_PLAN_V2_RAMSPLIT pool_gb=0.50 pool_share_of_memory_pct=3.1 pool_covers_corpus_pct=100.0 fill_stage_gb=0.12 leaf_stage_gb=0.03 arena_group_gb=14.24 finish_witness_gb=0.00 finish_pfck_grid_gb=0.00 usable_gb=14.40 rule=the pool is sized FIRST and pinned to the whole corpus text whenever --memory-gb allows (the hot set is the boilerplate epoch); the two staging buffers are constants per thread; the arena pair takes the remainder; the finish is a second process under the same cap and owns its witness stream + pfck grid
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN live_cap_slots=2088968 windows=1 window_file_gb=0.0 ram_group_gb=0.0 count_s=0 fill_s=0 build_s=0 stitch_s=0 producer_s=0 finish_s=0
XSA_PLAN_V2_TARGET rows=262144 leaves=8 levels_per_row=3.49 largest_leaf_rows<=262144 rule=subdivide-while-rows>target (depth is an OUTPUT of the census; the depth cap is a fail-loud backstop, not the rule)
XSA_PLAN_V2_POSITION_STORE window_file_gb=0.03 = credit(2) x cap(2088968) x 8 B ON DISC (one rolling file per live window, unlinked when built); ram_group_gb=0.03 = 16 B/slot x the group being sorted in place; position_io_gb=0.0 = 16 x n / (8+8) B a position written once and read once; position_io_s=0 at the 5.238 GB/s device floor (overlapped by the fill and the build, so not on the critical path); persistent_position_column=0 full_SA=0
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_END e2e_s=0 e2e=0:00:00 producer=0:00:00 finish=0:00:00 rule=max(producer,finish) (concurrent, flow-controlled through the piece window)
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_NOTE 1 windows = ceil(n/2088968) (each window re-reads the whole corpus: fill = windows x n at the 5.238 GB/s device floor = 0.00 h at this scale); bins are indivisible so a window is packed to <= cap by whole bins (every measured point matches ceil exactly: 1 GB cap 250M -> 5, 1 GB cap>=n -> 1); a single bin larger than the cap makes the producer raise it (BIN_CAP_RAISED) and the front door FAILS LOUD rather than price a different arena. The TREE: 8 leaves = ceil(n/target), each a comparison sort of <= 262144 rows (depth is an OUTPUT of the byte census; mean levels/row 3.49 measured at this target, i.e. the emergent depth is 0 for the busiest bucket, not a parameter). Terms (s/GB at 1 GB): count 1.360 fill 0.191+0.191/window build 107.930@4t stitch 11.408 = producer 120.89; finish 118.90 (own work); e2e = max = 120.89. Measured 1 GB producer wall 41.68 s and with-finish 142.18 s (flow-limited): the model holds the producer term to 290.0%
